      "hints": [
        "Set $\\frac{5k - 6}{3k} = \\frac{6k - 4}{5k - 6} \\implies (5k - 6)^2 = 3k(6k - 4)$.",
        "Expand and simplify to $7k^2 - 48k + 36 = 0$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Equate the common ratios of consecutive terms in the geometric progression:\n$$\\frac{5k - 6}{3k} = \\frac{6k - 4}{5k - 6}$$",
        "Cross-multiply and expand both sides:\n$$(5k - 6)^2 = 3k(6k - 4)$$\n$$25k^2 - 60k + 36 = 18k^2 - 12k$$",
        "Collect all terms on the left-hand side:\n$$25k^2 - 18k^2 - 60k + 12k + 36 = 0 \\implies 7k^2 - 48k + 36 = 0$$"
      ],
