      "hints": [
        "Solve $(7k - 6)(k - 6) = 0 \\implies k = \\frac{6}{7}, 6$.",
        "Find $r = -\\frac{2}{3}$ for $k = \\frac{6}{7}$, and $r = \\frac{4}{3}$ for $k = 6$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Factorise the quadratic equation in $k$:\n$$7k^2 - 48k + 36 = 0 \\implies (7k - 6)(k - 6) = 0$$\n$$k = \\frac{6}{7} \\quad \\text{or} \\quad k = 6$$",
        "Calculate the common ratio $r = \\frac{5k - 6}{3k}$ for each value of $k$:\n$$\\text{For } k = \\frac{6}{7}: \\quad r = \\frac{5\\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right) - 6}{3\\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)} = \\frac{\\frac{30 - 42}{7}}{\\frac{18}{7}} = -\\frac{12}{18} = -\\frac{2}{3}$$\n$$\\text{For } k = 6: \\quad r = \\frac{5(6) - 6}{3(6)} = \\frac{30 - 6}{18} = \\frac{24}{18} = \\frac{4}{3}$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
