      "hints": [
        "Identify convergent ratio $r = -\\frac{2}{3}$ with $a = 3\\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right) = \\frac{18}{7}$.",
        "Calculate $S_\\infty = \\frac{18/7}{1 - (-2/3)} = \\frac{54}{35}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "The geometric progression converges when $|r| < 1$, which corresponds to $r = -\\frac{2}{3}$ and $k = \\frac{6}{7}$:\n$$a = 3k = 3\\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right) = \\frac{18}{7}$$",
        "Calculate the sum to infinity:\n$$S_\\infty = \\frac{a}{1 - r} = \\frac{\\frac{18}{7}}{1 - \\left(-\\frac{2}{3}\\right)} = \\frac{\\frac{18}{7}}{\\frac{5}{3}} = \\frac{18}{7} \\times \\frac{3}{5} = \\frac{54}{35} \\quad (\\approx 1.54)$$"
